<title>MEXICO: Mexico's Bufete wins engineering project.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Bufete wins engineering project.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bufete Industrial, a specialist engineering, procurement and construction firm, said Friday it won a project with BASF Mexicana, a wholly-owned subsidiary of Germany-based chemicals giant BASF.</p>
<p>No financial terms were given for the project, which is to engineer and procure an ABS plant. ABS is a material needed for the automotive and electronic industries.</p>
<p>The plant, which will be located in Altamira, in Tamaulipas state, is designed to produce 130,000 tons of ABS per year to serve international markets.</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom (525) 7289530))</p>
